/-!
# Actual Griess (1990) elementary abelian 3^3 symmetry, rational 27D

Source: R. L. Griess Jr., J. Algebra 131 (1990), 281-293:
the F3³ 27 one-dimensional homogeneous character spaces of the ORIGINAL
Albert 27D algebra, NOT the Monster VOA weight-two Griess product.

A generator acts as omega^(a_r) on homogeneous e_a. In the tau-real
pair (e_a+e_-a, omega e_a+omega² e_-a) it has 2×2 matrix:
identity if a_r=0, [[0,-1],[1,-1]] if a_r=1,
[[-1,1],[-1,0]] if a_r=2. The distinguished e0 is fixed.
The three 27×27 rational source matrices below are exactly this
source-selected character action. The conjugates through the explicit
Griess→RationalAlbertNative 27×27 map are literal native-algebra actors.

Exact external local Python confirmed 3×729 native Jordan products;
27/27 group character traces, order 3, commuting action and Gram/unit.
Lean native_decide theorems below are SOURCE-WRITTEN, not kernel-run.
This does not provide F4 original-Q classification or a 27-site path
graph/Monster/physical/KK/RH equivariant intertwiner.
-/

